# madcide menu data (S1, 2026-09-08): the command / menu contribution —
# what a menu bar, a command palette, or any client that renders commands
# natively shows. The TUI reads none of it (JOE has no menu bar); the
# composed tree carries it as the root's `menu` hint.
#
# One line per item:    MENU  COMMAND  [{ICON [DROP]}]  TITLE...  [WHEN]
# A separator:          MENU  -
# MENU is the top-level menu the item belongs to (first appearance orders
# the bar). COMMAND is an action id from the ONE vocabulary the key
# profiles bind (profiles/*.keys) and the dispatcher understands — never a
# key spelling: a renderer shows the chord the LOADED profile binds to it.
# TITLE is everything after the command. An optional trailing [WHEN] names
# the context that must hold for the item to be enabled: a context key,
# `!key` to negate, `a && b` to join. Context keys: editable dirty
# selection split buffers project building modal viewing.
# An optional {ICON} is the picture a renderer draws for the item (ui::icon:
# new open save run debug stop step-over step-into step-out breakpoints); an
# unknown word refuses the menu. On a `toolbar` row a second word, {ICON
# DROP}, names the menu of this file the button's arrow drops down.
# The menu "palette" lists commands that live only in the command palette
# (a title for every command the bar does not carry).
# The Build menu's items after its separator are COMPOSED, not listed here:
# the ^B palette's rows (buildcmds — the built-ins for the buffer or the
# project, plus a manifest's own commands), one item per row, id build-<n>.

